A PREDICTION, NOT A RESULT: every capture below was taken for another question (PROGRESS.md P2-1).
corpus: 276 .log; loader boots 1 (cold 1, warm 0, ? 0); kernel boots 1 (vendor 0, rlxfw quiet 1, rlxfw loud 0, rlxfw ? 0, firmware unknown 0); kernel text without rtkload 0
rules: a byte arrived at the LAST .timing row with offset <= its own (FW-35), an upper bound; landmarks and cold/warm as in the tool's header; a cell is n, median (mean of the middle two when n is even), min..max, in seconds

landmarks, each table in its search order (THE SEARCH RULE in the tool's header); a kernel boot is searched with LOADER then its firmware's table;
`=` marks a landmark defined identically in VENDOR and RLXFW; `(?P<at>...)` is the byte a landmark sits on
  LOADER
     booting      Booting\.\.\.[\s\S]{2}(?P<at>[\s\S])
                    the byte after `Booting...\r\n`: anchor C, CLK-15's own
     chipname     chipName: 
                    the loader's `\0chipName: ` (a loud kernel's SPI table prints `chipName    |`, with no colon)
     ramsize      ramSize: 32M
                    C-8 reads the line after it
     banner       ---RealTek\(RTL8196E\)
                    the loader's banner (D1b)
     autoboot     Jump to image start=
                    printed only when no ESC arrived inside the window (LDR-15)
  VENDOR
   = jump         ---Jump to address=|Jump to image start=
                    the loader leaving for the image: a typed `J`, or its own autoboot
   = decomp       decompressing kernel:
                    rtkload, inside the image; the same text in both images
   = decomp_done  done decompressing kernel\.
                    rtkload
   = kentry       start address: 0x[0-9A-Fa-f]{8}
                    rtkload's last line before it enters the kernel
   = wlan         Realtek WLAN driver
                    the WLAN driver's banner: in both kernels, different builds
   = nic          Probing RTL8186 10/100 NIC
                    the NIC driver's probe
   = fastpath     Realtek FastPath:v1\.03
                    the FastPath module
     userinit     init started: BusyBox
                    the vendor's init, BusyBox 1.13.4
     ready        boa: starting server
                    the last line the vendor prints: its web server starting
  RLXFW
   = jump         ---Jump to address=|Jump to image start=
                    the loader leaving for the image: a typed `J`, or its own autoboot
   = decomp       decompressing kernel:
                    rtkload, inside the image; the same text in both images
   = decomp_done  done decompressing kernel\.
                    rtkload
   = kentry       start address: 0x[0-9A-Fa-f]{8}
                    rtkload's last line before it enters the kernel
     b00          RLXFW-B00
                    start_kernel, after page_address_init (config/rlxfw-marks.tsv)
     b09          RLXFW-B09
                    start_kernel, after console_init
   = wlan         Realtek WLAN driver
                    the WLAN driver's banner: in both kernels, different builds
   = nic          Probing RTL8186 10/100 NIC
                    the NIC driver's probe
   = fastpath     Realtek FastPath:v1\.03
                    the FastPath module
     b10          RLXFW-B10
                    init_post, before the branch that reaches userspace
     userinit     rlxfw: init running
                    the first line of rlxfw's /init (config/rlxfw-init.sh)
     ready        job control turned off\r?\n(?:[^\n]*\n){0,8}?(?P<at>#)(?= |\Z)
                    the `#` of the first prompt after the shell's own first line
segments -- interval = t(to) - t(from); absent (`--`) unless both landmarks are in the firmware's table and in the capture
  loader.booting       booting     -> chipname    identical       CLK-15: stage 1 copying out of SPI NOR; the loader table's `booting`
  loader.banner        booting     -> banner      identical       the loader table's `banner` (D1b); D2's positive control
  loader.esc           banner      -> autoboot    identical       LDR-15's ESC window; exists only when the loader autobooted
  rtkload.decompress   decomp      -> decomp_done comparable      scales with the image, whose size this tool does not read (D4)
  rtkload.total        jump        -> kentry      comparable      the loader's jump to rtkload's hand-over
  kernel.early         kentry      -> wlan        comparable      
  kernel.wlan          wlan        -> nic         comparable      the vendor's WLAN init, present in both kernels
  kernel.nic           nic         -> fastpath    comparable      
  kernel.late          fastpath    -> userinit    comparable      holds rlxfw's own 300-jiffy pre-check wait (CLK-27, IRQ-13)
  kernel.total         kentry      -> userinit    comparable      
  user.ready           userinit    -> ready       not-comparable  the vendor runs rcS and its daemons; rlxfw execs a shell
  boot.jump_to_ready   jump        -> ready       not-comparable  TERM-1's J -> ready
  rlxfw.setup          b00         -> b09         not-comparable  rlxfw only: start_kernel from page_address_init to console_init
  rlxfw.initpost       b10         -> userinit    not-comparable  rlxfw only: init_post to /init's first line

